-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2619eb87-a4d6-584a-ac06-7c0d135f7808" :question/math-academy-id "q-106876" :question/problem "![](images/95/952f35d03c8554f2feaeb50296df9ac426a49730a44038bf6f9cf47b1fa3f9ee.png)\n\nThe vector $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\frac{5}{2}.$ Find the vector $Av.$" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\frac{5}{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](images/cb/cb3fae2e42e90e7e8398c311fd9c4d20ac1db51687a7d4f3f77146eb53728de5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f5608f-a9f5-5e6a-b308-540ed8b29259" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given an Eigenvalue and Eigenvector of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000e3561-1544-5dc9-8c11-17c48b422a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284787} {:answer/id #uuid "097c3642-1c4d-5f84-8e55-34a351e7fb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284868} {:answer/id #uuid "0cd337c9-0e8e-5c98-801f-ee9718e01ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284893} {:answer/id #uuid "201af8ed-db42-5e03-815b-dbf694b92e78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285075} {:answer/id #uuid "fad2ed4b-35b0-525e-8240-933b2bc19e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201af8ed-db42-5e03-815b-dbf694b92e78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a631f2f2-9eef-524a-8c00-16323ea7e0c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac23d8ea-7894-5e1d-9e2b-923ff426fb50" :question/math-academy-id "q-18233" :question/problem "An eigenvector of $D=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 10 \\\\ -7 & 11\\end{bmatrix}$ corresponding to an eigenvalue $\\lambda =6$ is  $\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}.$ Determine the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $D$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Dv=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Dv & =\\lambda v \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 10 \\\\ -7 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} & =6\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-8c+140 \\\\ -7c+154\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6c \\\\ 84\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8c+140 &=6c \\\\ -7c+154 &=84\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-8c+140=6c\\,⟹\\,c=10.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-7c+154=84\\,⟹\\,c=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $c=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49c501da-161c-53be-8349-571cc6a07975" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting the Product of a Matrix and an Eigenvector Given its Corresponding Eigenvalue"