ath-academy-id "q-75734" :question/problem "![](images/02/0269c9d60a97984f55cefccbd8cf1192dfdb4082935162206b1ce1a3cfb413f7.png)\n\nThe vector $u$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $-1.$ Find the vector $Bu.$" :question/worked-solution "The eigenvector $u=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Bu & =-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](images/af/afc3e8503656a84f23c7f58fd05e005ee07200b75ddec1aa5cf247b3484e81b4.png)"}]}
